                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Game is Nothing Short than a masterpiece\nI have personal bias, being that this was one of my first games I ever played, back on the og xbox, But the remaster stays ever faithful to its original, with improvements such as higher fps and graphics.\nThe soundtrack is a melody to my ears as it sends you into a new orleans type setting, with hints of jazz.\nWhile not being the most complex platformer it stands out amongst its competitors in its overwhelming sense of style that the game presents at every opportunity it gets.\nWith the higher graphics, we players are handed with constant fps only varying at small points, which allows vinces movement to get to places further away compared to the original game with its lower fps count.\n\nI love this game to the very bottom of my heart, but no game is perfect and just like everything else in this world there are cons.\nVinces Shadow is very broken, a visual error, but isn't a bad thing\nYou store voodoo powers through the amount of powerskulls you've collected, but if you fall into a ditch or water you lose your entire stock, which can be a bit annoying sometimes\nI'm sure theres other cons to point out, I'm just too blinded by nostalgia.\n\nI heavily recommend checking out this game as it is just such a great platformer, especially for its time in 2001\nalso! the game doesn't hold your hand like crazy like most newer games, so have fun with that!",
